    "notes": [
      "Paper carries no elevation and no motion. Both arrays above are empty on purpose, not unfilled: the theme separates with rules and space, and a dialog is the one surface that floats, with a hairline and a scrim rather than a shadow.",
      "Four rules in the Paper sheets are written as `box-shadow: inset 2px 0 0 var(--accent)`. They draw a 2px rule where a border would change an element's box, so they are geometry, not elevation.",
      "Classic still ships as the default preset and does carry shadows and transitions. They are deliberately not recorded here: this sidecar describes the system new work is written against, and DESIGN.md names classic frozen.",
      "Tonal ramps are synthesized preview metadata at each colour's own chroma and hue. The shipped token is `canonical`; a ramp step is not an application token.",
      "A scrim is the one colour with no ramp: it ships as a translucent black, and a ramp of it would describe the paper underneath rather than the colour itself.",
      "Component snippets below are documentation previews with values inlined from the Paper dark preset. The application reads them as custom properties, which switch with the preset."
    ]
  },
  "components": [
    {
      "name": "Action word",
      "kind": "button",
      "refersTo": "action-word",
      "description": "There are no buttons in Paper. An action is a word with a 1px green rule under it. The word that completes a screen is the same word at 600; a quiet action drops the rule; a destructive one is clay and stays clay on hover.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-actions\"><button class=\"ds-act\">add task</button><button class=\"ds-act ds-act--completing\">add project</button><button class=\"ds-act ds-act--quiet\">open</button><button class=\"ds-act ds-act--danger\">delete</button></div>",
      "css": ".ds-actions{display:flex;gap:24px;align-items:baseline;background:#1b1a19;padding:16px}.ds-act{padding:0;border:0;background:transparent;color:#e8e5df;font:400 15px/1.6 Literata,Georgia,serif;text-align:left;text-decoration:underline 1px #8fd18a;text-underline-offset:.2em;cursor:pointer}.ds-act:hover:not(:disabled){color:#8fd18a;text-decoration-color:#8fd18a}.ds-act--completing{font-weight:600}.ds-act--quiet{color:#a39e96;text-decoration:none}.ds-act--danger,.ds-act--danger:hover:not(:disabled){color:#e8907c;text-decoration-color:#e8907c}.ds-act:focus-visible{outline:2px solid #8fd18a;outline-offset:3px}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Row",
      "kind": "list-item",
      "refersTo": "row",
      "description": "A list is rows separated by a hairline, never cards. `now` carries a 2px green rule at its left; `done` is muted and struck through; late metadata turns amber. Figures in metadata are tabular.",
      "html": "<ul class=\"ds-rows\"><li class=\"ds-row ds-row--now\">Return the library books<span class=\"ds-meta\">due sep 15</span></li><li class=\"ds-row\">Problem set 3<span class=\"ds-meta ds-meta--late\">sep 12</span></li><li class=\"ds-row ds-row--done\">Send the venue confirmation</li></ul>",
      "css": ".ds-rows{list-style:none;margin:0;padding:16px;background:#1b1a19}.ds-row{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:baseline;gap:16px;padding:12px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #3b3936;background:transparent;font:400 17px/1.6 Literata,Georgia,serif;color:#e8e5df}.ds-row--now{border-left:2px solid #8fd18a;padding-left:12px}.ds-row--done{color:#a39e96;text-decoration:line-through}.ds-meta{font:400 13px/1.5 Literata,Georgia,serif;color:#a39e96;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.ds-meta--late{color:#e0b565}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Section heading",
      "kind": "heading",
      "refersTo": "heading",
      "description": "A section within a page, with the green `// ` that opens it. This is the one place the accent appears without marking position.",
      "html": "<h2 class=\"ds-heading\">appearance</h2>",
      "css": ".ds-heading{margin:0;padding:16px;background:#1b1a19;font:600 17px/1.3 Literata,Georgia,serif;color:#e8e5df;text-wrap:balance}.ds-heading::before{content:\"// \";color:#8fd18a}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Field",
      "kind": "input",
      "refersTo": "field",
      "description": "The one place Paper draws a box, because a field has to say where typing goes. 6px corners, a 1px outline, the raised ground.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-wrap\"><input class=\"ds-field\" placeholder=\"what needs doing\"></div>",
      "css": ".ds-wrap{padding:16px;background:#1b1a19}.ds-field{width:100%;padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #7d7972;border-radius:6px;background:#252422;color:#e8e5df;font:400 17px/1.6 Literata,Georgia,serif}.ds-field::placeholder{color:#a39e96}.ds-field:focus-visible{outline:2px solid #8fd18a;outline-offset:3px}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Checkbox",
      "kind": "checkbox",
      "refersTo": "checkbox",
      "description": "Drawn, not filled: the box keeps the page's ground and only the tick is green, because a filled green square would read as a state and green only ever means here. 18px, and `padding: 0` against the classic `input` rule.",
      "html": "<label class=\"ds-check-row\"><input class=\"ds-check\" type=\"checkbox\" checked> Work and study</label>",
      "css": ".ds-check-row{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;padding:16px;background:#1b1a19;font:400 17px/1.6 Literata,Georgia,serif;color:#e8e5df}.ds-check{appearance:none;-webkit-appearance:none;display:inline-grid;place-content:center;width:18px;height:18px;flex:none;margin:0;padding:0;border:1px solid #7d7972;border-radius:2px;background:#252422;cursor:pointer}.ds-check::before{content:\"\";width:10px;height:5px;border-left:2px solid #8fd18a;border-bottom:2px solid #8fd18a;transform:translateY(-1px) rotate(-45deg);visibility:hidden}.ds-check:checked::before{visibility:visible}.ds-check:focus-visible{outline:2px solid #8fd18a;outline-offset:3px}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Navigation item",
      "kind": "nav",
      "refersTo": "navigation",
      "description": "Where you are is a 2px green rule under the word, and the word in full ink. Everything else is muted. No pill, no fill.",
      "html": "<nav class=\"ds-nav\"><button class=\"ds-nav-item ds-nav-item--current\">current</button><button class=\"ds-nav-item\">active</button><button class=\"ds-nav-item\">someday</button></nav>",
      "css": ".ds-nav{display:flex;gap:16px;padding:16px;background:#1b1a19}.ds-nav-item{padding:8px 0;border:0;border-bottom:2px solid transparent;background:transparent;font:400 17px/1.6 Literata,Georgia,serif;color:#a39e96;cursor:pointer}.ds-nav-item:hover{color:#8fd18a}.ds-nav-item--current{color:#e8e5df;border-bottom-color:#8fd18a}.ds-nav-item:focus-visible{outline:2px solid #8fd18a;outline-offset:3px}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Dialog",
      "kind": "dialog",
      "refersTo": "dialog",
      "description": "The one surface that floats: the raised ground, a 1px hairline, 6px corners, at most 520px, over a scrim. No shadow. Its actions sit at the end of the last line, the completing one at 600 and cancel quiet beside it.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-scrim\"><div class=\"ds-dialog\"><h2 class=\"ds-dialog-title\">new task</h2><p class=\"ds-dialog-body\">It will go to today unless you give it a date.</p><div class=\"ds-dialog-actions\"><button class=\"ds-act ds-act--quiet\">cancel</button><button class=\"ds-act ds-act--completing\">save task</button></div></div></div>",
      "css": ".ds-scrim{padding:24px;background:rgba(0,0,0,.55)}.ds-dialog{max-width:520px;padding:24px;border:1px solid #3b3936;border-radius:6px;background:#252422;color:#e8e5df}.ds-dialog-title{margin:0 0 24px;font:600 20px/1.3 Literata,Georgia,serif;letter-spacing:-.005em}.ds-dialog-body{margin:0 0 24px;font:400 15px/1.6 Literata,Georgia,serif;color:#a39e96}.ds-dialog-actions{display:flex;gap:24px;justify-content:flex-end;align-items:baseline}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Error banner",
      "kind": "alert",
      "refersTo": "error",
      "description": "A 2px clay rule at the left and the sentence beside it. No box, no fill. Retry is an action word in clay, and stays clay on hover, because green there would say the opposite of what the banner means.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-wrap\"><div class=\"ds-error\">We could not reach your tasks. <button class=\"ds-error-retry\">retry</button></div></div>",
      "css": ".ds-error{display:flex;gap:8px 12px;align-items:baseline;margin:16px 0;padding:0 0 0 12px;border:0;border-left:2px solid #e8907c;border-radius:0;background:transparent;font:400 15px/1.6 Literata,Georgia,serif;color:#e8907c}.ds-error-retry{min-height:0;padding:0;border:0;border-radius:0;background:transparent;font:400 15px/1.6 Literata,Georgia,serif;color:#e8907c;text-transform:lowercase;text-decoration:underline 1px #e8907c;text-underline-offset:.2em;cursor:pointer}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Calendar event",
      "kind": "list-item",
      "refersTo": "event-rule",
      "description": "An event is a name with its time and place under it, and a 1px rule at its left carrying the Google calendar's own colour. Nothing is filled, so nothing shouts. Figures are tabular.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-wrap\"><div class=\"ds-event\" style=\"--event-rule:#7986cb\">Library study<span class=\"ds-event-meta\">7:30pm – 12:30am · Fictional campus</span></div></div>",
      "css": ".ds-event{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px;padding:0 0 0 8px;border-left:1px solid var(--event-rule,#7d7972);background:transparent;font:400 13px/1.5 Literata,Georgia,serif;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;color:#e8e5df}.ds-event-meta{color:#a39e96}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "Paper, Not Chrome",
    "overview": "apraxia is one person's workspace, so it reads like their own page rather than a product someone shipped at them. Paper is the theme that does that: warm paper in two presets, Literata throughout, hairlines instead of card edges, and words instead of buttons. Nothing is filled, nothing floats but a dialog, and nothing moves. The one colour with a job is a green that marks where you are. Classic remains the default preset and is frozen as it is; Paper is what new work is written in.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Rules, not boxes: a 1px hairline separates rows where another interface would draw a card.",
      "Words, not buttons: an action is a word with a green rule under it.",
      "One green, one meaning: the accent marks where you are and the action that completes a screen, and is never used as decoration or as a fill.",
      "Literata throughout, at seven sizes and two weights, in both presets.",
      "No shadow, no gradient, no motion, no pill.",
      "Interface words are lowercase; the account's own words keep their case."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Green Means Here Rule",
        "body": "The accent marks position — today's column, the current page, the current-time line — and the one action that completes a screen. It is never a fill and never decoration. A destructive word stays in `danger` even on hover, because turning it green would say the opposite of what it does.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Rules Not Boxes Rule",
        "body": "Separation is a 1px hairline and space. A dialog is the only surface that floats, and it floats with a hairline and a scrim rather than a shadow. `elevation` and `motion` in this sidecar are empty because the theme has neither.",
        "section": "elevation"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Words Before Icons Rule",
        "body": "An action is its own word. Icons ride beside a word rather than replacing it; the two calendar chevrons are the one icon allowed to stand alone.",
        "section": "components"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Lowercase Interface Rule",
        "body": "Interface words are lowercase, and they are lowercased in the Paper sheet with `text-transform`, never by editing a string both themes render. An element that mixes interface words with the account's own content is not a candidate.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Sibling Sheet Rule",
        "body": "Every Paper rule lives in a sibling `*Paper.css` scoped `[data-theme^=\"paper\"]`, which matches both presets and never matches classic. A classic sheet is never edited, so classic stays pixel-identical while Paper is built beside it.",
        "section": "overview"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Classic Globals Rule",
        "body": "`index.css` carries unscoped `input`, `button` and `select` rules that apply under Paper too. A Paper rule only wins a property it names, and `font` is a shorthand that silently resets weight. Clear every property you care about, and guard an exclusion with `:where(:not(...))` rather than `:not(...)`, which carries its argument's specificity.",
        "section": "components"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do read tokens from `paper.css` and scope every rule `[data-theme^=\"paper\"]`.",
      "Do reach for `.paper-action`, `.paper-row`, `.paper-field`, `.paper-check`, `.paper-nav__item`, `.paper-dialog`, `.paper-error` and `.paper-event` before writing a new primitive; escalate a missing one rather than inventing a local copy.",
      "Do let a calendar event's rule carry that calendar's own colour, which is Google's data rather than a token.",
      "Do keep figures that line up in columns on `tabular-nums`.",
      "Do keep a visible focus ring: 2px `accent`, 3px offset, and the same shape everywhere.",
      "Do measure with computed styles in the QA fixture rather than judging by eye."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't add a shadow, a gradient, a transition or a pill. If something needs separating, give it a rule or space.",
      "Don't fill anything with the accent, or use it to decorate. It means here.",
      "Don't edit a classic sheet or a shared string to make Paper look right; the fix belongs in a Paper sheet.",
      "Don't draw a weight other than 400 or 600; Literata ships only those two, and anything else is synthetic.",
      "Don't treat the signed-out screen's Space Grotesk and JetBrains Mono as part of the system: that screen predates both themes and is not themed.",
      "Don't use `.paper-field`'s `background` shorthand on a `select` without restoring the chevron; the shorthand wipes the background image the classic rule draws it with."
    ]
  }
}
